From: hIRoic Linux hammer PoC <noreply@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tty: stm32-usart: thread non-DMA interrupts on PREEMPT_RT

The STM32 USART driver registers an explicit IRQF_ONESHOT primary handler,
so PREEMPT_RT's forced-thread setup deliberately leaves that primary handler
in hard-IRQ context.  The non-DMA TX path takes uart_port.lock, which is a
sleeping spin lock on PREEMPT_RT and triggers scheduling-while-atomic.

For the non-DMA case, register the complete USART handler as the explicit
thread function on PREEMPT_RT.  Preserve the existing split hard/threaded
DMA handling and preserve all non-RT behavior.

Upstream-status: Pending
---
 drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c | 13 +++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c b/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/stm32-usart.c
@@ -827,12 +827,19 @@ static int stm32_usart_startup(struct uart_port *port)
 	struct stm32_port *stm32_port = to_stm32_port(port);
 	const struct stm32_usart_offsets *ofs = &stm32_port->info->ofs;
 	const struct stm32_usart_config *cfg = &stm32_port->info->cfg;
+	irq_handler_t handler = stm32_usart_interrupt;
+	irq_handler_t thread_fn = stm32_usart_threaded_interrupt;
 	const char *name = to_platform_device(port->dev)->name;
 	u32 val;
 	int ret;
 
-	ret = request_threaded_irq(port->irq, stm32_usart_interrupt,
-				   stm32_usart_threaded_interrupt,
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_PREEMPT_RT) &&
+	    !stm32_usart_rx_dma_enabled(port)) {
+		handler = NULL;
+		thread_fn = stm32_usart_interrupt;
+	}
+
+	ret = request_threaded_irq(port->irq, handler, thread_fn,
 				   IRQF_ONESHOT | IRQF_NO_SUSPEND,
 				   name, port);
 	if (ret)
